  "knowledge": "The framework rolls the transaction back, and PostgreSQL confirms the ROLLBACK, so the client knows that nothing committed.",
  "api_outcome": {
    "reported": "rolled_back",
    "basis": "the body returned an error and sql.Tx.Rollback returned nil",
    "contract": "Go database/sql Tx.Commit returns the error from driver.Tx.Commit and does not add a command tag (database/sql/sql.go). pgx stdlib v5.11.0 wrapTx.Commit calls pgx.Tx.Commit and returns that error (stdlib/sql.go). A nil error is database/sql's report that the transaction committed. pgx.ErrTxCommitRollback therefore reaches the caller as a non-nil error. stdlib Conn.ResetSession returns driver.ErrBadConn when pgx's transaction status is not idle, so the pool discards that connection before the next checkout. database/sql has no savepoint type. This control sends SAVEPOINT, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT, and RELEASE SAVEPOINT as SQL.",
    "error": {
      "class": "*errors.errorString",
      "code": null,
      "message": "application error: the request fails"
    },
    "steps": {}
  },
